chezmoi:modify-template
{{- /* Cap every model whose catalog advertises more than 128k at 128k.
     Compaction keys off the advertised window, so an uncapped session grows
     past the point where these models stay coherent and cheap.

     modelOverrides keys are exact provider model IDs, not patterns, and pi
     has no global cap, so the IDs are enumerated: the union of
     `pi --list-models` and the hyper, cline-pass, and commandcode catalogs in
     exact_extensions/exact_providers. tests/repo/test_pi_models.py re-derives
     that union from the catalogs, so a catalog that gains a model above the
     cap fails the suite until the ID is listed here. Unknown IDs are ignored
     by pi, so a retired entry is harmless. Paths are lists because the IDs
     contain dots and slashes. Everything else in models.json, including
     custom providers and other override fields, is preserved. */}}
{{- $current := fromJson (.chezmoi.stdin | default "{}") }}
{{- $cap := 131072 }}
